#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:11
msgid "Telegram Fleet Roll Call Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:13
msgid "Problem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:15
msgid ""
"Each Hermes gateway filters incoming messages by `allowed_users` in its "
"config.yaml. If Agent A sends a message to Agent B's bot, Agent B sees it"
" as coming from Agent A's bot user ID, not Agent B's allowed user. "
"Without cross-listing, agents can't reply to each other and roll calls "
"fail silently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:20
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:22
msgid "1. Discover all bot user IDs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:57
msgid "2. Update each agent's config.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:59
msgid "Edit `platforms.telegram.allowed_users` in every agent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:68
msgid "3. Restart all gateway processes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:74
msgid "Verify running:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:79
msgid "Should return the expected number of agent processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:81
msgid "4. Verify roll call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:83
msgid ""
"Send a message to ALL bots simultaneously. Each bot should now reply "
"because they recognize the sender (which is another bot's user ID, now in"
" their allowed_users)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:86
msgid "5. Check pairing for new bots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:88
msgid "When a new bot is first started, it may need pairing approval:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:93
msgid ""
"The code is printed by the bot when it first receives a message from an "
"unknown user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:95
msgid "Pitfalls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:97
msgid ""
"**Restart required:** Changing `allowed_users` does NOT take effect until"
" the gateway process restarts. There is no hot-reload for this setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:99
msgid ""
"**Quote the string:** `allowed_users` must be a string in YAML, use "
"`'ID1,ID2,ID3'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:100
msgid ""
"**Don't forget the human user:** The human user's chat_id (5837518218) "
"must remain in the list, or they lose access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:102
msgid ""
"**Each machine is separate:** If agents are spread across machines "
"(command, ai, laptop), you must update configs on each machine "
"separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/telegram-fleet-roll-call_SKILL.md:104
msgid ""
"**Roll call delivery:** Use `cronjob(action='list')` to find the roll "
"call cron job and check its `deliver` target. If it delivers to `origin`,"
" it sends back through whatever channel the user contacted from."
msgstr ""

